{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Reconfirmed on current origin/main at 070c54e6f0ff34577c3cb66632d57387f7bddf7d. Makefile, pyproject.toml, and tests/unit/test_worktree_python_pin.py are unchanged from the original 25d1d683e55a reproduction. /opt/homebrew/bin/uv --version reports 0.12.9, the repository still requires uv ==0.12.7, and the venv recipe still handles every uv venv failure with the Python-unavailable diagnostic. The reported bug remains present on origin/main.","timestamp":1788589172639709001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Reconfirmed on current origin/main at c019920390926d543a0813d4c0c8721543d98776. The relevant Makefile, pyproject.toml, and tests/unit/test_worktree_python_pin.py have not changed since the previous reproduction. The selected /opt/homebrew/bin/uv is 0.12.9, the repository still requires uv ==0.12.7, and the Makefile still maps every nonzero uv venv result to the Python-unavailable diagnostic. The bug remains present.","timestamp":1788594633976497001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Reconfirmed on current origin/main at 0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e. Makefile, pyproject.toml, and tests/unit/test_worktree_python_pin.py are unchanged from the prior c0199203 reproduction. /opt/homebrew/bin/uv is 0.12.9, the repository requires uv ==0.12.7, and the make venv recipe still maps every nonzero uv venv result to its Python-provisioning diagnostic. The bug remains present.","timestamp":1788606392083984001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"2026-09-05 reconfirmation on origin/main@d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84: the repository requires uv 0.12.7, this host provides /opt/homebrew/bin/uv 0.12.9, and the current Makefile still reports a generic missing-Python diagnosis for any uv-venv failure. This is the requested uv-version-mismatch bug; no duplicate was created.","timestamp":1788626835794236001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Confirmed on origin/main@4c9940348148fb255b17ddf1cb124701ad4565d7: make worktree name=comment-gates-current created the branch/worktree, then failed provisioning because the repository requires uv==0.12.7 while the host uv is 0.12.9. The target left the worktree with no usable .venv and exit 2. Non-global workaround succeeded: uvx --from uv==0.12.7 uv venv --python 3.12 .venv; uvx --from uv==0.12.7 uv sync --locked --extra dev --extra metrics; env PATH=\"/Users/joeoakhart/comment-gates-current/.venv/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/opt/homebrew/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/System/Cryptexes/App/usr/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/var/run/com.apple.security.cryptexd/codex.system/bootstrap/usr/local/bin:/var/run/com.apple.security.cryptexd/codex.system/bootstrap/usr/bin:/var/run/com.apple.security.cryptexd/codex.system/bootstrap/usr/appleinternal/bin:/pkg/env/global/bin:/opt/homebrew/opt/ruby@3.4/bin:/opt/homebrew/lib/ruby/gems/3.4.0/bin:/Users/joeoakhart/.codex/tmp/arg0/codex-arg0spyp95:/Applications/ChatGPT.app/Contents/Resources:/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:/opt/homebrew/opt/python@3.14/libexec/bin:/Applications/Visual\\ Studio\\ Code.app/Contents/Resources/app/bin:/opt/homebrew/opt/postgresql@17/bin:/usr/local/opt/postgresql@17/bin:/Users/joeoakhart/.local/bin:/Users/joeoakhart/.lmstudio/bin\" make hooks. This confirms the mismatch is a current-main bootstrap defect, not stale-branch behavior.","timestamp":1788634663522142001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Reconfirmed on origin/main@1d60c5f72ff008ddc3acdff42fd5b84ecdfb2752. Makefile, pyproject.toml, and tests/unit/test_worktree_python_pin.py are unchanged since the prior reproduction. The repository requires uv==0.12.7, the selected Homebrew uv is 0.12.9, and the Makefile still reports this uv refusal as a Python-provisioning failure. The bug remains present; no duplicate was created.","timestamp":1788655093159969888},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Starting implementation pass. Read ticket/RCA and prior reconfirmation comments; proceeding to plan review before claim per workflow.","timestamp":1788755047026430001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review blocked on the test sandbox not staging pyproject.toml for the required-version preflight. Amended the plan to require copying pyproject.toml into the real-Makefile subprocess sandbox, then re-running plan review once per workflow.","timestamp":1788755803732831001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review passed after one description amendment; claimed ticket and starting isolated worktree implementation.","timestamp":1788756279084014001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented and committed fix 9b7922e13701 in isolated worktree fix4-foliated. RED oracle: tests/unit/test_worktree_python_pin.py::test_make_venv_reports_uv_version_mismatch_before_python_hint failed before production change with the generic Python provisioning hint. GREEN: tests/unit/test_worktree_python_pin.py passed after the Makefile preflight. Starting full make verify.","timestamp":1788756598145168001}],"created_at":1788584510722419001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"39f4e277-7272-4601-ba3d-be2f870d4b9d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3e32-a859-2153-4a1b"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nOn `origin/main` at `25d1d683e55a`, `make worktree name=comment-remediation-3e32` selected `/opt/homebrew/bin/uv` 0.12.9 while `pyproject.toml` requires 0.12.7. `uv venv` correctly refused the mismatch, but the Makefile catch-all handler reported that Python 3.12 was unavailable and advised `uv python install 3.12`. Running the same target with the existing 0.12.7 binary created a Python 3.12.13 venv, proving that diagnosis false.\n\nThe exact uv pin and its refusal are intentional. This bug is the misleading classification of every `uv venv` failure as a missing interpreter. It is distinct from `princely-courageous-milksnake`, which repairs the machine-local updater uv selection.\n\n## Approach\nKeep fail-fast provisioning. Add a preflight that compares the selected uv executable/version with the repository exact required version before `uv venv`, and emit a mismatch-specific diagnostic naming the executable, actual version, and required version. Preserve the existing interpreter-unavailable diagnostic for a compatible uv whose venv operation fails.\n\nExtend the real-Makefile subprocess tests with controlled uv stubs for both failure classes. The subprocess sandbox must copy `pyproject.toml` as well as the Makefile and `.github/python-version.txt`, so the new preflight reads the same `[tool.uv].required-version` source in tests that production `make venv` reads.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A selected uv version that violates `[tool.uv].required-version` fails before provisioning and names the selected path, actual version, and required version.\n- [ ] The mismatch path does not claim Python is unavailable or advise installing the already-available pinned interpreter.\n- [ ] A compatible uv whose `uv venv --python <pin>` fails still reports the pinned-interpreter provisioning failure.\n- [ ] `make worktree` continues to propagate either provisioning failure without printing its success message.\n- [ ] Focused Makefile worktree/python-pin tests, lint, and typecheck pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"Makefile","reason":"Classify selected uv version mismatch separately from interpreter provisioning failure."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_worktree_python_pin.py","reason":"Drive the real Makefile with uv stubs covering incompatible-version and interpreter-unavailable diagnostics."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"71a122b9-c52b-4a7c-93c8-bb6f8103f4e2","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["devex","makefile","diagnostics","uv"],"ticket_id":"1f58-ba19-afac-445e","ticket_type":"bug","title":"make worktree misreports a uv version mismatch as a missing Python interpreter","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d31b54f2-27b2-4c7e-abf1-bc822061b69d","c7aecfb5-b580-4e9d-86c2-f8c2748f8450","2e2a5dee-79ab-471d-aa20-7294a5b4805a","79bd6a55-e438-4fd4-981e-a91e620d9131","e0e87024-ce42-42df-9f8d-e53468cea21a","117570fd-20c3-46cf-8ebd-38daacc2bf8d","9188c47b-b912-402a-b6f6-9088ac1f3aae","37532b82-e311-4e1f-a92e-10fb3e45ee40","c19303db-f7ec-4616-ad64-a9cde9c21bf8","e66a7678-f423-4f76-85c7-7e44af4a72a8","71a122b9-c52b-4a7c-93c8-bb6f8103f4e2","acdb2f57-e884-4cdf-acdd-f9b65cfc806a","e4bb675f-4190-473f-adbc-d7eb6a11939c","771a9bcd-e1c6-4720-baae-be9e2657c114"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788756598145168002,"uuid":"cb144ca4-c2aa-4aea-9ec9-05a4f8040604"}